```

## SNS Fan-out → Multiple SQS Queues

```
Order Service
    │ publishes to
    ▼
[SNS Topic: order-events]
    ├──→ [SQS: inventory-queue]     → Inventory Service
    ├──→ [SQS: notification-queue]  → Email/Push Service
    └──→ [SQS: analytics-queue]     → Analytics Service
```

## Spring Boot: Send to SQS

```java
@Service
public class OrderEventPublisher {
    private final SqsTemplate sqsTemplate;

    public OrderEventPublisher(SqsTemplate sqsTemplate) {
        this.sqsTemplate = sqsTemplate;
    }

    public void publishOrderCreated(Order order) {
        OrderCreatedEvent event = new OrderCreatedEvent(order.getId(), order.getCustomerId(),
            order.getTotalAmount(), Instant.now());
        sqsTemplate.send("order-events-queue", event);
    }
}
```

## Spring Boot: Consume from SQS

```java
@Service
public class InventoryConsumer {

    @SqsListener(value = "inventory-queue", acknowledgementMode = MANUAL)
    public void processInventoryUpdate(
            OrderCreatedEvent event,
            Acknowledgement ack) {
        try {
            inventoryService.reserveItems(event.getOrderId());
            ack.acknowledge();  // delete message from queue
        } catch (InsufficientStockException e) {
            log.error("Insufficient stock for order {}", event.getOrderId());
            // DON'T acknowledge — message becomes visible after visibility timeout
            // After maxReceiveCount retries → goes to DLQ
        }
    }
}
```

## DLQ Configuration

```java
// After 3 processing failures, message goes to DLQ
// Configure via AWS Console or CloudFormation:
// redrive_policy: {deadLetterTargetArn: inventory-dlq-arn, maxReceiveCount: 3}

@SqsListener("inventory-dlq")
public void handleDeadLetter(OrderCreatedEvent event) {
    log.error("DEAD LETTER: order {} could not be processed", event.getOrderId());
    alertingService.notify("Dead letter received: " + event.getOrderId());
    // Store for manual investigation
    deadLetterRepo.save(new DeadLetterRecord(event));
}
```
